 subgroups of one-relator groups"},{"area":null,"id":"scope:GroupTheory/presentations-and-decision-problems/generic-properties-of-group-presentations","kind":"scope","lean":null,"status":"can_prove","summary":null,"title":"Generic properties of group presentations"},{"area":null,"id":"GroupTheory/presentations-and-decision-problems/higman-infinite-simple","kind":"node","lean":"MathlibExt.GroupTheory.HigmanInfiniteSimpleWanted.GroupTheory.HigmanInfiniteSimpleProblem.higman_infinite_simple","status":"can_prove","summary":"There exist a natural number $n$ and a finite set $R$ of elements of the free group on generators $x_1, \\dots, x_n$ such that the group $\\langle x_1, \\dots, x_n \\mid R \\rangle$ presented by these generators and relators is simple and infinite.","title":"Infinite finitely presented simple groups exist"},{"area":null,"id":"GroupTheory/presentations-and-decision-problems/higman-neumann-neumann-embedding","kind":"node","lean":"MathlibExt.GroupTheory.HNNEmbeddingWanted.higman_neumann_neumann_embedding","status":"fully_proved","summary":"Every countable group $G$ embeds in a group generated by two elements: there are a group $H$, elements $a, b \\in H$ that generate $H$, and an injective group homomorphism $f \\colon G \\to H$.","title":"Higman–Neumann–Neumann embedding theorem"},{"area":null,"id":"scope:GroupTheory/presentations-and-decision-problems/involutions-in-quotient-groups","kind":"scope","lean":null,"status":"can_prove","summary":null,"title":"Involutions in quotient groups"},{"area":null,"id":"GroupTheory/presentations-and-decision-problems/is-squniversal","kind":"node","lean":"MathlibExt.GroupTheory.SQUniversalShared.IsSQUniversal","status":"fully_proved","summary":"A group $G$ is SQ-universal if every countable group is isomorphic to a subgroup of a quotient of $G$: for every countable group $C$ there are a group $Q$, a surjective homomorphism $G \\to Q$ and an injective homomorphism $C \\to Q$.","title":"SQ-universal group"},{"area":null